hifiberry-vu-meter (0.1.4) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix a memory/CPU leak that could starve the whole device after about a
    day of uptime (#1). The realtime PipeWire capture callback blocked on a
    plain mutex that the (non-realtime) level-processing thread held while
    computing RMS/peak/clipping, so contention showed up as capture xruns in
    the tens of millions; the capture callback now try_locks and drops a
    period rather than blocking. The shared per-channel buffer also only
    ever shrank (`clear`/`drain`), never releasing capacity gained under
    contention, letting its peak size become a permanent floor; it is now
    preallocated to a fixed cap that samples are dropped rather than grown
    past.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 05:59:54 +0000

hifiberry-vu-meter (0.1.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * The service reports its own version again. 0.1.2 shipped a binary that
    answered /api/v1/version with "0.1.0": the release bumped
    debian/changelog but not Cargo.toml, and the version the binary reports
    comes from Cargo.toml at compile time. A deployment could therefore not
    be told apart from one that had silently kept the previous binary --
    which is the one thing that endpoint exists to answer.
  * Carry the version into Cargo.lock's entry for the crate as well. It was
    left at 0.1.0 when Cargo.toml was corrected, so every package build
    rewrote the entry and left the checkout dirty afterwards -- and a
    --locked build would have failed outright rather than proceeded.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 05:36:27 +0000

hifiberry-vu-meter (0.1.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Ship the auth-gateway classification manifest (etc/hifiberry/auth.d/vu-meter.json).
    The VU meter is a read-only audio-level stream, so the whole service is
    "ok" (never prompts for a password). Previously the manifest existed only
    as an on-device file shipped by no package.
  * Fix the Rust build under sbuild: add curl + ca-certificates to
    Build-Depends (debian/rules rustup-installs the toolchain via curl, absent
    from the chroot), and point RUSTUP_HOME at a writable build-dir path — the
    sbuild build user's HOME is /sbuild-nonexistent, so rustup's default
    $HOME/.rustup could not be created.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Fri, 17 Jul 2026 14:00:00 +0000

